From 31f9eab644fbe0f9aa270e36b0d7c078c2bdb2ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:27:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/40] fix(python-client): no pending leak on surrogates, no
 shared-process kill on id:null, closed pool stays closed

* PC-01: encode the request before registering it in _pending; a lone
  surrogate is now EngineError (was UnicodeEncodeError + leaked slot).
* PC-10 (FS-4): reject requests the engine cannot parse at text level
  (non-str dict keys -> duplicate keys after json.dumps; nesting > 256,
  FormatIO.maxDepth) before sending: the engine answers those with
  {"id":null,...}, which the client must treat as a protocol violation and
  which killed the shared process and every neighbour's in-flight request.
  RecursionError from json.dumps is also EngineError now.
* PC-02: Engine.close() marks the pool closed; later calls raise EngineError
  instead of silently spawning engine processes that nobody closes.
* PC-03: failure to spawn a replacement process (missing binary, EACCES,
  EMFILE) is EngineError, not a raw OSError.
* PC-12: SIGKILL the process group only once, on the first failure, before
  the background wait() can reap it; close() marks the process so the
  reader's EOF does not killpg an already reaped (free) pid.

Regression: client_robustness.py R5-R9 red on baseline, green now;
client_faults.py, client_contract.py, host_sim.py, loadtest.py still green.

(cherry picked from commit 51c31ce1e06f2d697b19fc98e38e8050c98ee436)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JgWRtX2jyUidN8gxEhe5qx
